1727 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1726 0 R
  /Alt (Two comparative maps display Urban Atlas Green Urban Areas (GUA) in Iasi, Romania, showing classification by access type and recreational use, based on data from 2018 to 2021. Both maps share the same legend and overlaid polygon features. The top map uses a street map as the base layer, while the bottom map uses high-resolution satellite imagery. The legend defines the polygon outlines: * Blue outline: `14110 - public` * Red outline: `14120 - private` * Purple outline: `14130 - unknown` * Green outline: `14200 - Recreational Areas` Both maps include a scale bar indicating 0.1 km and 0.2 km, and a north arrow. The maps highlight various urban green spaces, classifying them by their access status. Multiple large areas are delineated as `14110 - public` (blue outline), some of which contain or are adjacent to `14200 - Recreational Areas` (green outline), such as sports fields and parks. Smaller, often more fragmented areas, are classified as `14120 - private` (red outline) or `14130 - unknown` (purple outline), particularly within more densely built-up urban sections. The `ro502l1_iasi_ua2018_2021` label likely refers to the product identifier for the Urban Atlas Green Urban Areas in Iasi.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [4]
  /Pg 2588 0 R
>>
endobj

